I don't think that Matt was talking about your weapon preference, but
rather on your statement "some useless kind of weapon". A weapon that
hits "harder than most artifacts" is far from being useless. You may
get a different view once you try it out and compare it to the damage
done by other weapons. There is still the valid point (which you have
not mentioned) of the disadvantage of a cursed two-handed weapon, but
that would mainly be an issue in the later game when monsters will be
able to curse your stuff. Getting a mattock in the early game, mainly
in the mines, is a good start to build up your game.

With reference to your preference of a shield of reflection; yes, that's
indeed a good choice. Though I am sure shields of reflection are much
rarer than mattocks in the mines. And the chance to get reflection by
an amulet is much higher, 50% to be exact, since that's the probability
for the Sokoban price.

